The `min_elements_to_remove(data)` function uses a bit mask to efficiently calculate the sum of the remaining elements after removing specified elements. It iterates over all possible subsets of the input list and checks if the sum of the subset is a prime number. If it is, and the number of elements to remove is less than the current minimum, it updates the minimum number of elements to remove and the indices of the elements to be removed.

